cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "healpix-convert: converting Earth-observation and climate data to a HEALPix DGGS in Zarr"
abstract: >-
  Tools for converting Earth-observation and climate datasets from their native
  gridded formats onto the HEALPix discrete global grid, written as Zarr. Data is
  resampled onto HEALPix cells at one or more refinement levels, and the output
  carries the metadata needed to interpret it: the DGGS-Zarr and multiscales Zarr
  conventions, a CF grid mapping and cell methods, and STAC discovery and
  provenance records describing how each dataset was produced. Converters for
  ERA5, CAMS and DestinE ClimateDT are included, on top of a generic conversion
  core that is agnostic of the data product being converted.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/GRID4EARTH/healpix-convert"
keywords:
  - HEALPix
  - Discrete Global Grid Systems
  - DGGS
  - Zarr
  - CF conventions
  - STAC
  - resampling
  - Earth observation
  - ERA5
  - CAMS
  - ClimateDT
  - GRID4EARTH
